# GitHub fork and PR habit (tvscreener-rs)

## Ownership

| Role | Account / org | Duty |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Canonical (upstream)** | [Interchouette-ITC](https://github.com/Interchouette-ITC) | Owns `tvscreener-rs`. **Integration branch = `dev`.** Merge only via PR. |
| **Worker fork** | [Interchouette](https://github.com/Interchouette) (SSH `github.com-itc`) | Forks upstream, **feature branches**, opens **PRs into Interchouette-ITC `dev`** |
| **Personal** | Greg (`gRoussac`, …) | **Approve** = merge gate (same idea as publications BAT). Not the day-to-day worker remote |

## Branches (locked habit)

| Branch | Where | Role |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **`dev`** | Org + fork | **Only** default / integration branch |
| **`feat/…` `fix/…` `docs/…` `chore/…`** | **Fork only** | Day-to-day work. One concern per branch. Deleted after merge. |

Do **not** recreate `main` as the integration branch once org remotes exist.

## Commits (signed + conventional)

- Author: **Interchouette** `<contact@interchouette.net>` (local repo `user.*`, not Greg's global).
- **Sign every commit** with SSH key `~/.ssh/id_ed25519_itc` (`gpg.format=ssh`, `commit.gpgsign=true`).
- Never commit as Greg's personal identity on this worker repo.
- Subject grammar: see `github-public-quality.mdc`.

## Merge style (fork rebase + squash)

| Step | Who / where | Action |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Keep PR current | **Fork** | `git fetch interchouette && git rebase interchouette/dev` on the feature branch, then push to `interchouette` (SSH-signed). |
| Reviewer | Every PR | Always `--reviewer gRoussac` |
| Merge gate | **gRoussac Approve** | Comments = babysit only. Never merge without Approve. |
| Land on org | After Approve | `gh pr merge --squash` with conventional PR title as the squash subject. |
| Forbidden default | Agent | `gh pr merge --rebase` onto org (GitHub rewrites commits and drops Verified). |

```bash
gh pr create --repo Interchouette-ITC/tvscreener-rs --base dev --head Interchouette:<feat> --reviewer gRoussac
# or on an existing PR:
gh pr edit <n> --repo Interchouette-ITC/tvscreener-rs --add-reviewer gRoussac
```

CODEOWNERS: `* @gRoussac` in repo-root `CODEOWNERS` (`.github/` is the local creds symlink, gitignored).

## Workflow (every change)

```text
fork: create feat/… from interchouette/dev
 → signed conventional commits + push interchouette feat/…
 → rebase onto interchouette/dev on the fork if behind (signed)
 → gh pr create --repo Interchouette-ITC/tvscreener-rs --base dev --head Interchouette:<feat> --reviewer gRoussac
 → confirm PR head Verified
 → wait gRoussac Approve, then --squash
 → sync fork: git fetch upstream && git checkout dev && git merge --ff-only upstream/dev && git push interchouette dev
 → prune local
```

1. Prefer **create under Interchouette-ITC**, then **fork to Interchouette**.
2. Day-to-day remote **`interchouette`** = fork; **`upstream`** = org. Do **not** name the worker remote `origin`.
3. **Never** `git push upstream`. Org code lands **only** by PR merge.
4. On the **fork**, commit and push freely to `interchouette`.

## Bootstrap

Done: org [`Interchouette-ITC/tvscreener-rs`](https://github.com/Interchouette-ITC/tvscreener-rs), fork [`Interchouette/tvscreener-rs`](https://github.com/Interchouette/tvscreener-rs), remotes `upstream` + `interchouette`, default branch `dev`.

Day-to-day work uses the workflow above. Do **not** invent a second integration branch.

## Do not

- Merge without **gRoussac** Approve.
- Open a PR without requesting **gRoussac**.
- Rely on Cursor chat alone for Approve (use GitHub review + `--reviewer gRoussac`).
